Z||000000||Max The Chainsaw||02-13-2001||09:34 PM||||Went to one of local salvage yards the other day. Picked up a full set of Factory Aluminum mags with Goodyear Eagles from an 86 SE for my 86 coupe. Cost $75.00.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Went to all 6 Fiero's they had and pulled out 3 Tach filters. They gave me the tach filters, thought they were condensers for an old distributor.  hehehe  Checked what they had, there's an 86 GT pretty well picked over but still has the 120 MPH guage set.  Maybe next time.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Al in all, a good day.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||BN Boomer||02-13-2001||09:59 PM||||That sucks! It's hard to even find a Fiero in a wrecking yard around here!<P>Oh well, good for you!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>You have my envy.||||reg||8
Z||000002||87GT||02-13-2001||10:08 PM||||A junkyard near me had 9 fieros in it.  8- 4 Bangers and 1- 6 banger.  5 were 84s, 1 88 coupe, 2-87 coupes, and one 86SE V6.  The cars were all pretty much stripped.  The SEV6 still had its motor in it, but that was about it.||||reg||1
